 3}=\\frac{21}{12}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{21}{12}=\\frac{21÷3}{12÷3}=\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nSo, Adam ate $\\frac{7}{4}\\,\\text{oz}$ of candy."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dda2934c-c5e6-50c3-b0c2-cb44becc1207" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying an Improper Fraction by a Proper Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "598b9672-1d4b-52e7-bb6d-9bc3e875ed0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{5}$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476397} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ef10dc-df61-575d-8c9c-a7db077f7d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{4}$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476621} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ffb7cc-5c6c-5476-bf5c-606f9749f685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{5}$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476644} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6dda2a-785b-538d-abb1-302ee4a122de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{5}$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476662} {:answer/id #uuid "d045739f-6f61-5628-b1f6-ebf2810909b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{3}$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb6dda2a-785b-538d-abb1-302ee4a122de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{5}$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476662} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecfd6f0-954e-5beb-a170-004c18aed877" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28a686c1-c2a4-5d2b-a982-8cf069fee2eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-91630" :question/problem "Max needs to solve all of the exercises in $\\frac{3}{2}$ pages of a math book. If he has already solved $\\frac{2}{5}$ of the exercises, how many pages of exercises has Max solved?" :question/worked-solution "To find out the number of pages Max solved, we need to calculate $\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nTo multiply the two numbers, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{2\\times 3}{5\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{10}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{10}=\\frac{6÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, Max solved $\\frac{3}{5}$ pages."}]}
